THOUGHT: The diff shows my change removed the original dereference error but introduced two new “passing @Nullable parameter 'texture' where @NonNull is required” errors at SpriteBatch.java:629 and CpuSpriteBatch.java:763, where switchTexture is called. To keep behavior and satisfy NullAway, I should restore the @Nullable annotation on switchTexture’s parameter and instead add an explicit null check before dereferencing texture inside switchTexture. That way, callers can still pass null, but the method won’t dereference it. After updating SpriteBatch.java accordingly, I’ll re-run the gdx compile and then re-check the NullAway error count to ensure it’s back to 453 (one less than the original dereference error, with no new ones added).

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '1159s/protected void switchTexture(Texture texture)/protected void switchTexture(@Nullable Texture texture)/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/SpriteBatch.java && sed -i '1160,1163c\    flush();
    lastTexture = texture;
    if (texture != null) {
      invTexWidth = 1.0f / texture.getWidth();
      invTexHeight = 1.0f / texture.getHeight();
    }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/SpriteBatch.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep "error: \\[NullAway\\]" new_build_output.log | wc -l && grep -n "SpriteBatch.java:1162" new_build_output.log || echo "SpriteBatch 1162 error not present"
```

